From 29666581f2a4c4f6402b7776077faa712e4e8a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add real PWA manifest, icons and offline service worker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The manifest was previously generated at runtime as a data: URI, which
browsers cannot use as an install target (a data: URL has no base, so
"start_url": "." never resolves) and it declared no icons, so the app
could not be installed on a phone.

- manifest.json: name/short_name/description, start_url and scope "./"
  (works on any hosting path, incl. GitHub Pages), standalone display,
  theme #10b981 on #f8fafc background, lang uk, categories, and
  shortcuts for "Мої за сьогодні" / "Всі списання" / "Пошук".
- icons/: generated 192 and 512 px icons in both "any" and "maskable"
  variants, plus a 180 px iOS icon and 16/32 px favicons, replacing the
  external logo URL that could not load offline.
- tools/generate_icons.py: reproducible source of those icons.
- sw.js: caches the app shell so the app opens without a connection;
  network-first for navigation, cache-first with background refresh for
  static assets, and Google Apps Script requests are never cached.
- index.html: links the real manifest and local icons, registers the
  service worker in secure contexts, and handles the ?view= parameter
  used by the manifest shortcuts.

Verified in Chromium: manifest parses without errors, all icons resolve
at their declared sizes, Page.getInstallabilityErrors is empty, and the
page still loads with cached data after going offline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019oBDMHmykBynwPxbchFmWn
